WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.131
SCP-507 – otherwise known as the Reluctant
Dimension Hopper – is an anomaly with a

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:07.131
rare condition.

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:10.780
Don’t worry though, it’s not contagious…
we think.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:16.190
No, this otherwise seemingly ordinary fellow
possesses a rather unpredictable anomalous

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.470
trait: he can travel to other dimensions.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.199
That sounds great, in theory, right?

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:26.199
Who among us wouldn’t want to visit alternate
universes and see worlds beyond our wildest

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:27.199
imaginations?

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:33.780
Well, the problem is that SCP-507 can’t
actually control this ability, it’s not

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.050
something he can do on a whim or by thinking
about it.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.720
Instead, he is relocated to other universes
seemingly at random, which can prove pretty

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.469
intrusive during an average Day in the Life
of SCP-507.

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:52.690
6:00 AM
It was still early, far too early for SCP-507

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.690
to be awake.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:58.050
But even while he slept, the Foundation was
making sure they had the necessary measures

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.250
in place to keep him comfortably contained.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.229
Or at least, until he next disappeared.

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:08.910
“Your assignment, Officer Dalton,” the
security chief said boredly, sliding a file

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:09.910
across the desk.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:12.440
“You want me to be the handler for this…

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.460
‘Reluctant Dimension Hopper’?”

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.070
Dalton replied after she had skimmed through
the file in front of her.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:23.619
“Special Containment Procedures for SCP-507
clearly dictate that an agent must be present

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:29.030
with the anomaly whenever he leaves his private
quarters,” the chief answered with a sigh,

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.030
having barely sipped his morning coffee.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:37.040
“Just keep an eye on him, do what he asks
as long as his requests don’t violate internal

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.040
security.”

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.950
“Sir, with respect,” Dalton cleared her
throat.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.610
“This feels like a waste of my talents.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:47.149
I’m as combat proficient and well-trained
as all other security operatives.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:52.030
Why do you want me playing day-care for someone
who’s own files refer to him as ‘sporting

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.860
no outstanding characteristics’?

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.979
“What, you thought we’d hire you and immediately
put you in the pen with 682?”

00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:00.280
the security chief scoffed.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.369
“Don’t look a gift horse in the mouth,
Officer.

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:05.579
This posting is a blessing, believe me.

00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:10.060
I’ve given agents just as competent as you
tougher posts and the number of them who died

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.060
on the job…

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.180
well, let’s just say it makes it easier
being up this early in the day.”

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.360
“But, sir, I could be doing more!”

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.370
“Trust me, start small.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:24.580
You’ll have your hands full with SCP-507,
he might not seem like much, but he’s slippery,”

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.580
the chief said.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.010
“You mean, he’ll attempt to escape?”

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.010
Dalton asked.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.040
The facility’s head of security didn’t
give an answer, instead he dismissed the officer

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.680
to her posting.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.260
Making her way through the corridors towards
SCP-507’s containment cell, Officer Dalton

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.550
studied her briefing, reading it through multiple
times so she understood her assignment.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:49.840
She was expecting her charge to be unruly,
attempting escape at any opportunity.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:55.580
What she had overlooked, in her haste, was
that SCP-507 wasn’t intentionally using

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.990
his dimension hopping powers to escape.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.490
In fact, he couldn’t help it.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.349
8:00 AM
Eventually growing tired of waiting outside

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:07.959
the entrance to the Reluctant Dimension Hopper’s
quarters, Officer Dalton began repeatedly

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:10.819
banging her fist against the door.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:13.920
“SCP-507, wake yourself up!” she yelled
impatiently.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.680
There came the sound of tired groaning from
the other side of the door, followed by something

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.330
person sized falling over in a daze.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.510
Getting to its feet, the source of the noise
shuffled closer and opened the door, all while

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.060
Dalton kept knocking.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:34.250
“That’s very loud, you know,” SCP-507
groaned, eyes half-lidded, practically still

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.250
asleep.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.200
“I’m your new handler,” the Officer
announced plainly.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:42.100
“Goody for you,” the Dimension Hopper
yawned.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.480
“I’m tired and going back to sleep.”

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.120
“Like hell you are!”

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.840
Dalton snapped, striding into the room.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.540
“I’ve been waiting outside for two hours!”

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.980
“Look, miss,” SCP-507 sighed.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.290
“I get the Foundation has to keep an eye
on me in case I…”

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.709
He made a gesture with his hands, jazzily
shaking them.

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:02.569
“You get the picture,” he continued.

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:05.790
“But I’m normally in bed for the first
half of the day.”

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:08.400
“First of all,” Dalton replied sternly.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.220
“I’m an officer in the Foundation.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.860
As such, you’ll refer to me as ‘Officer
Dalton’ or ‘Ma’am’, is that clear?”

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.609
She didn’t give 507 a chance to answer.

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:21.860
“Secondly, make no mistake: I’m not your
babysitter.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.040
I’m here to ensure the Foundation’s continued
security, not yours.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.820
And if one of your escape attempts poses a
threat to this organisation, then I am authorised

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.640
to carry out a termination order.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.320
In short, don’t screw around with me.”

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.660
SCP-507 looked sheepish, like a schoolchild
who’d just been told off by the principal.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.450
“So, am I right in thinking you like to
go by nicknames?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.880
What do I call you?”

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:50.930
He paused for a second, a cheeky smirk crawling
onto his face as he figured out a way he could

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.389
slyly mess with the no-nonsense officer.

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:59.050
“You can call me Grabnok the Destroyer,”
SCP-507 replied.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:03.470
Officer Dalton rolled her eyes: this was clearly
going to be a long day.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.580
10:00 AM
Sure enough, the newly appointed handler’s

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:12.199
first cause for concern came when SCP-507
suddenly blinked out of existence while brushing

00:05:12.199 --> 00:05:13.199
his teeth.

00:05:13.199 --> 00:05:18.210
She’d urged him to get himself ready and
freshened up, and no sooner had ‘Grabnok’

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:23.400
stepped into the bathroom, he’d disappeared,
his toothbrush clattering into the sink.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.360
Officer Dalton stared in disbelief at the
spot where he had just been, bowled over by

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.810
how brazen and how quickly the anomalous interdimensional
traveller had tried to give her the slip.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:37.759
Immediately, Dalton went to raise the alarm,
only to be ineffectively reassured by her

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:38.759
superiors.

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:43.140
‘This kind of thing happens all the time’
and ‘He’ll reappear soon, just keep sweeping

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.729
the facility until he shows up’ were all
she was met with.

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:50.020
And they did little to quell Dalton’s frustration.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:54.949
Eventually, SCP-507 reappeared, wandering
around one of the corridors of the Foundation

00:05:54.949 --> 00:05:59.389
facility and whining about a headache that
usually accompanied his dimensional displacement.

00:05:59.389 --> 00:06:02.229
“What the hell are you playing at vanishing
like that?”

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:03.229
Dalton barked.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:07.139
“I need to eat something,” Grabnok groaned,
ignoring her question.

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:10.710
“I displaced before breakfast; it always
makes me nauseous when it’s on an empty

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.710
stomach.”

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.139
“That’s your primary concern right now?”

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:15.560
the Officer sighed.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.080
“Well, yeah,” SCP-507 shrugged.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:22.389
“There was no food in that other dimension,
at least none that I could find.”

00:06:22.389 --> 00:06:27.060
Begrudgingly pushing aside her frustration,
Dalton escorted Grabnok to the Foundation

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.060
mess hall.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.960
“What else was there, SCP-507?”

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.560
she asked, breaking the silence as he ate
quietly.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:36.100
“I’ll have to file a report about where
you went.”

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.280
“Not answering to that,” he chuckled.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.850
“You’ve got to use the nickname.”

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.509
“Seriously?”

00:06:41.509 --> 00:06:42.819
Dalton replied.

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:47.330
“Okay, fine, what else was in that universe,
Grabnok?”

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.360
“The whole thing.”

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.660
“Grabnok the Destroyer,” she added through
gritted teeth.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.889
“Not a lot honestly,” the Dimension Hopper
shrugged.

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:01.289
“Some universes are just like that, this
one just had one big salt plane and nothing

00:07:01.289 --> 00:07:02.289
else.”

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:03.289
“You mean like a desert?”

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.289
Dalton probed.

00:07:04.289 --> 00:07:08.470
“No, a salt plane,” Grabnok corrected
her.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.479
“You know, like a glass salt shaker you’d
have at a fancy dinner table?

00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:13.740
Except with wings.”

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:17.960
“And what was in the… salt plane?”

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:18.960
she asked, confused.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:24.430
“I think it was white pepper,” SCP-507
answered sarcastically.

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:28.990
12:00 PM
After he had finished his meal, SCP-507 seemed

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.599
to be feeling better, and requested to be
taken back to his quarters to use his computer.

00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:38.139
He’d been granted one by the Foundation,
with limited internet access and a strict

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:40.840
limit on what he could access and upload.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:45.400
However, it was while escorting him back that
Officer Dalton realized her charge had once

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.430
again relocated while her back was turned.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:52.900
Dalton once again proceeded to traverse the
facility’s corridors, checking in with other

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:57.919
security staff and telling her fellow personnel
to keep her posted if SCP-507.

00:07:57.919 --> 00:08:04.400
Meanwhile, unbeknownst to her, the Reluctant
Dimension Hopper had found himself in a particularly

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.190
unique situation.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:12.550
Arriving in a new alternate universe, SCP-507
was greeted by familiar headaches, standing

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:16.449
in a spot that mirrored the Foundation site
he had been in a moment before.

00:08:16.449 --> 00:08:21.110
In fact, most of the details about this universe
were almost identical to the one he had just

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.110
left…

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.220
apart from all the dinosaurs.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:28.919
It quickly became apparent, at the sight of
a velociraptor wearing a lab coat, that this

00:08:28.919 --> 00:08:33.910
was a reality where the meteor that wiped
out early life on Earth had never actually

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:34.910
hit.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.539
As a result, the reptiles that had inhabited
the world centuries before had been able to

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:45.519
evolve into the dominant species, while humanity’s
earliest ancestors had never climbed out of

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:47.899
the primordial soup.

00:08:47.899 --> 00:08:53.310
SCP-507 found himself in a facility overrun
with reptilian researchers, all working for

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:57.480
an organization called the ‘Scaly Carnivorous
Predator Foundation’.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:02.420
Naturally, the dinosaurs were fascinated by
the sudden and inexplicable existence of this

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.620
pink, fleshy creature appearing out of thin
air.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:10.610
Although, the researchers working at this
version of the Foundation were similarly well-versed

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.079
in the study of the anomalous.

00:09:13.079 --> 00:09:18.790
Unfortunately, there was something of a language
barrier between SCP-507 and the dinosaurs

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.130
of this dimension.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:25.150
A kind, calm request for him to come quietly
so the research reptiles could run tests ended

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:28.310
up sounding like a vicious, bloodthirsty snarl.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.660
And so, the Reluctant Dimension Hopper turned
heel and ran away from a flock of raptors

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:38.990
in Foundation lab coats, until he eventually
displaced back to his original dimension again.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:43.890
1:30 PM
“Right, sure they did, 507,” Dalton sighed

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:48.529
after her charge had reappeared and recounted
his story of sentient dinosaurs running an

00:09:48.529 --> 00:09:50.040
alternate version of the Foundation.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.600
“And I bet Jeff Goldblum and Laura Dern
were both public enemies in this universe

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.600
too.”

00:09:55.600 --> 00:10:01.440
“I wasn’t in Jurassic Park,” SCP-507
argued, his head splitting.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.380
“I could have been eaten alive if those
raptors caught up to me!”

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:09.740
Officer Dalton helped the blonde haired and
green eyed dimensional traveler to his feet,

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:12.550
and began marching him towards a debriefing
room.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:18.440
As part of their continued research into not
only SCP-507 but the wider multiverse, the

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:23.730
Reluctant Dimension Hopper often had to describe
his unplanned expeditions after the fact.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.680
“Screw that, I almost died!” he protested.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:30.490
“I don’t want to go and give a debrief,
I’ll do it later.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.589
It’s got to be past lunch time in this universe,
right?” he asked.

00:10:33.589 --> 00:10:37.160
“You eat after debrief,” Dalton insisted.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.089
“Nah, I want lunch,” SCP-507 retorted.

00:10:40.089 --> 00:10:41.700
“I need to recharge.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.510
I’ll go and sit with Fernand!”

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:47.829
Reluctantly, remembering she’d been told
to do whatever the Dimension Hopper asked,

00:10:47.829 --> 00:10:52.380
Officer Dalton changed course and walked him
towards the enlarged containment area housing

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.710
SCP-082.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:58.769
‘Fernand’ was genetically an ordinary
human being who had grown into a giant through

00:10:58.769 --> 00:11:01.160
some unknown means.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:06.300
Given that SCP-507 was usually permitted to
freely interact with must other relatively

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:12.110
harmless anomalies, he had developed something
of a friendship with SCP-082.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:16.860
As a result, Grabnok considered his visits
to be a vacation of sorts.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:21.170
Despite Fernand’s grotesque appearance,
the giant was actually very friendly, especially

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.670
towards SCP-507.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:28.370
The creature’s body was dense with muscle
and fat, heavily scarred and his face disproportioned

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.529
to the rest of him.

00:11:29.529 --> 00:11:36.990
Yet, both SCP-082 and SCP-507 seemed to converse
jovially and enjoyed each other’s company

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:38.149
over lunch.

00:11:38.149 --> 00:11:42.870
That is, until the Reluctant Dimension Hopper
unceremoniously displaced again, midway through

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:47.100
talking to his giant friend about his latest
multiversal excursion.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:52.220
SCP-082 turned to Officer Dalton the second
Grabnok had vanished and shrugged casually.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:53.780
“He does that.”

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.960
4:00 PM
Over the course of the next few hours, at

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:03.160
least as the time passed in his home dimension,
SCP-507 was relocated into a universe where

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.209
everyone on Earth was a sentient hot dog.

00:12:06.209 --> 00:12:11.380
It was a jarring change to adapt to, although
not quite as initially frighting as encountering

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.860
the dinosaurs on his previous outing.

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:18.510
The hot dog population were a bit more guarded
that the inhabitants of the last universe

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:24.449
he’d been to, but after ensuring them that
he meant no harm, SCP-507 quickly established

00:12:24.449 --> 00:12:25.870
a rapport with some of them.

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:30.850
The first question he had was whether, like
the dinosaurs, these anthropomorphic baseball

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:36.310
stand snacks had naturally evolved into the
dominant species over time.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:42.430
SCP-507 was surprised to learn that, in actuality,
these hot dog creatures had previously been

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:47.220
human, until a strange plague had befallen
them several hundred thousand years prior.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:51.150
Ironically, this had all taken place before
their civilisation had even developed the

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:54.000
practice of eating sausages in bread.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:58.420
“Okay, so let me follow that up with another
question,” SCP-507 declared.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:02.959
“Make it quick man, I’m late for work,”
the large talking hot dog replied.

00:13:02.959 --> 00:13:07.829
“So, when you all changed into hot dogs,
did you really become sausages then develop

00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:09.220
bread coats to wear?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.510
Or are you both?”

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.959
“Wait, what do you mean?”

00:13:11.959 --> 00:13:13.270
the hot dog person replied.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.260
“You know, because technically a hot dog
isn’t a hot dog unless you put it in a bread

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.750
roll,” SCP-507 explained.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:25.699
“So are you all actually sausages, or are
you like coalescent beings of both sausage

00:13:25.699 --> 00:13:26.950
and bread?

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:31.871
The ensuing political unrest, civil turmoil
and ethical outcry that overtook the hot dog

00:13:31.871 --> 00:13:37.880
dimension following SCP-507’s question made
him really glad he displaced back home not

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.130
long after.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:43.610
He couldn’t help feel a little disheartened
too; up until the hot dogs were trying to

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:48.940
place him over a giant grill, SCP-507 had
actually found that he’d been enjoying the

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.620
time he spent there.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:56.029
Still, he was grateful to be back in a universe
populated by actual humans once again, even

00:13:56.029 --> 00:14:00.950
if the first one he met upon returning – Officer
Dalton – was furious that he’d been gone

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.220
for so long.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:06.529
7:00 PM
“You know, I’m wise to your act,” she

00:14:06.529 --> 00:14:07.529
replied.

00:14:07.529 --> 00:14:12.079
SCP-507 had just requested dinner, although
for some reason pointed out that he wanted

00:14:12.079 --> 00:14:14.870
to avoid eating hot dogs for a while.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.450
“What act?” he asked.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.950
“This thing you do, your disappearing act,”
the Officer responded.

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:24.949
“You’re not this bumbling interdimensional
traveller, you’re just an immature brat,

00:14:24.949 --> 00:14:25.949
SCP-507.”

00:14:25.949 --> 00:14:28.000
“You have to call me-”
“Grabnok the whoever!

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:32.900
Or Tommy, or Guy, or whatever the hell your
name is at this precise moment in time!”

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:36.899
Dalton snapped angrily, forcing SCP-507 to
go silent.

00:14:36.899 --> 00:14:39.090
“You just teleport, that’s what you do.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:43.889
You zip out of one place and reappear in the
next, and give personnel like me a run around.

00:14:43.889 --> 00:14:47.709
And it’s a hoot, it’s just a big joke
you can pull on us.

00:14:47.709 --> 00:14:51.260
That would be bad enough, if you didn’t
come back with these absurd stories on top

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.260
of it.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.260
What’s next, huh?

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.029
A dimension where the Foundation is run by
cats?

00:14:55.029 --> 00:14:57.080
Or a world where everyone is a sentient fart?”

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:01.360
“I don’t make it up,” SCP-507 replied
meekly.

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:06.520
“The place I end up in are real, I don’t
get to pick where I displace to or how weird

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.940
it is when I get there.”

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:11.580
“No, I said that I’ve figured you out,”
Dalton retorted.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:16.329
“You make up some wild story, these fool
yarns you keep spinning to confuse people.

00:15:16.329 --> 00:15:18.589
Then, you can request anything you want.

00:15:18.589 --> 00:15:23.120
That’s your real anomalous trait, Grabnok
the Destroyer, you’re able to pull the wool

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:25.890
over our eyes and use it to garner special
privileges.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:29.540
A computer, almost total freedom to roam around
the Foundation at will.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:31.360
Food and board, anything you want you get.”

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.790
There was a long, awkward pause.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.880
SCP-507 looked miserable.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:41.440
He was aware that, as cruel as she was being,
Officer Dalton’s anger was born more out

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.519
of frustration than anything else.

00:15:43.519 --> 00:15:46.680
He couldn’t help his interdimensional displacement
disorder.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:50.670
Sure, it had meant the Foundation offered
him certain treatment someone might consider

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.670
to be preferential.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:56.630
But he was still trapped, not so much by the
facility or even the Foundation themselves.

00:15:56.630 --> 00:16:03.910
Instead, SCP-507 was trapped by his condition,
unable to freely choose which universe he

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:04.910
stayed in.

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:09.199
8:00 PM
Dalton had escorted SCP-507 to debrief, then

00:16:09.199 --> 00:16:10.779
back to his quarters.

00:16:10.779 --> 00:16:14.319
The entire time, an air of uncomfortable silence
followed them.

00:16:14.319 --> 00:16:18.110
She still wasn’t entirely convinced that
her charge’s anomalous ability wasn’t

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:20.630
all a sham – at least in part.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:24.720
But standing guard at his bedroom door, she
could see him sulkily browsing the internet

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.110
on his computer.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:30.760
He was quiet, and Dalton couldn’t help that
it did make her feel a little bad for losing

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.589
her temper at him earlier.

00:16:32.589 --> 00:16:37.029
“Hey, SCP-507,” she said, poking her head
through the doorway.

00:16:37.029 --> 00:16:40.830
He didn’t respond, mindlessly scrolling
without turning around.

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:46.569
Stepping inside, Dalton closed the gap between
them by walking towards SCP-507, sat in his

00:16:46.569 --> 00:16:48.060
computer chair.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:53.160
“Listen, SCP-507,” she repeated, then
realising why he wasn’t replying or paying

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.160
her any notice.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:59.839
With a roll of her eyes and a heavy, exasperated
sigh, Officer Dalton readdressed the Reluctant

00:16:59.839 --> 00:17:03.490
Dimension Hopper: “Hey, Grabnok the Destroyer.”

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:09.360
Hearing that made SCP-507 turn around in an
instant, giving her his full attention.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:12.860
“Ma’am,” he said, still sulking but
at least willing to speak.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:16.240
“I’m very sorry for what I said before,”
Dalton admitted.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:20.339
“I don’t enjoy this, you know,” SCP-507
said solemnly.

00:17:20.339 --> 00:17:24.730
“One minute I’m somewhere familiar, the
next I’m thrust into some horrible nightmare

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:30.030
where everyone’s got macaroni cheese for
hands, or there are so many spiders everywhere.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.620
It’s not a joke to me, and it sucks!”

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:38.090
There were tears in the Dimension Hopper’s
eyes, and Officer Dalton reached out to pat

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.140
him on the shoulder.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:43.580
“I know, and I’m sorry for saying you
made it all up,” she offered a smile.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.550
Then, in the blink of an eye, they were both
gone.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:51.059
10:00 PM
Every other time that SCP-507 had displaced

00:17:51.059 --> 00:17:55.840
during the day, the Foundation had barely
paid it any mind, not even reacting when Officer

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.990
Dalton had brought it to their attention.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:02.610
But the moment she had disappeared along with
the Reluctant Dimension Hopper, security staff

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:05.080
and researchers went into a frenzy.

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:10.280
Alarms were sounded, personnel were patrolling
the corridors en masse, sweeping room to room

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:15.940
with flashlights in the hope not only that
SCP-507 would return… but that Officer Dalton

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.190
would still be with him when he did.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:22.870
It had been a few hours since the pair of
them had vanished, the sun had long since

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.130
sent and night had fallen.

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:30.490
Yet, there was still no sign… until a researcher
heard the sound of someone sobbing coming

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:32.669
from one of the storage closets.

00:18:32.669 --> 00:18:36.880
Calling it in, a trio of Foundation security
cautiously approached the closet and threw

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:43.140
open the door, only to find SCP-507 sat inside,
weeping floods of tears.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:47.270
Immediately, despite how late at night it
was, the Reluctant Dimension Hopper was told

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:52.350
he needed to debrief on where he had just
been, and what had happened to his handler,

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:53.590
Officer Dalton.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:58.610
SCP-507 began to describe displacing to a
dimension he had visited a number of times

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:04.179
before, a reality that was shrouded in complete
darkness, no sunlight at all.

00:19:04.179 --> 00:19:10.270
A familiar sound had instantly told the Reluctant
Dimension Hopper where he was and that he

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:11.270
wasn’t alone.

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:14.480
Doubly so, because Officer Dalton’s hand
had been on his shoulder.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:18.309
Completely by accident, she had transported
there with him.

00:19:18.309 --> 00:19:23.650
Switching on the flashlight he took with him
everywhere, SCP-507 was horrified to see a

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.880
figure who had tormented him before.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:31.799
He wore a black business suit, the matching
sunglasses he had on made the figure resemble

00:19:31.799 --> 00:19:33.409
a ‘man in black’ agent.

00:19:33.409 --> 00:19:39.970
It leered at him and Officer Dalton with an
unnaturally wide smile that had haunted SCP-507’s

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:42.390
nightmares ever since their first encounter.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:47.040
“Back again,” the figure had said, leaning
in towards SCP-507.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:51.500
“And this time you’ve brought a friend…”

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:56.540
“He took her,” the Reluctant Dimension
Hopper said quietly as he sat in the debriefing

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.540
room.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.010
“The Smiling Man got her.”

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:03.760
“We better get you cleaned up and sent to
bed, SCP-507,” one of the researchers said,

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.620
forcing a reassuring smile.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.060
“We’ll assign you another new handler
in the morning.”

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:13.770
Now go and check out “SCP-507 RELUCTANT
DIMENSION HOPPER” and “CAN SCP-096 CHASE

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.909
ITS VICTIMS ACROSS THE MULTIVERSE?”

00:20:15.909 --> 00:20:20.690
for more background on the man who can traverse
the multiverse… and quite literally can’t

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:21.389
stop.

